      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{5},\\,g=3 x^{4} + x^{3}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=5g^{4},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=12 x^{3} + 3 x^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=5g^{4}\\cdot (12 x^{3} + 3 x^{2}) \\\\  &=5(3 x^{4} + x^{3})^{4}(12 x^{3} + 3 x^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
